Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.78,0:06:15.91,Alt Overlap,,0,0,0,,Awesome! Awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.66,0:00:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did I put it...?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.13,0:00:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I know it's in here somewhere...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.25,0:00:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh...?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.43,0:00:16.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.88,0:03:41.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.09,0:03:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.95,0:04:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Rajdhani!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.79,0:04:19.25,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this? Something Indian?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.97,0:04:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You two are going home, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.93,0:04:25.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.14,0:04:31.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, would you let me lend you a hand?\NI know I can be of some help to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.39,0:04:35.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, we'd love that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.81,0:04:38.52,Default,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.52,0:04:41.32,Default,,0,0,0,,...says that about 2,000 years\Nhas passed, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.32,0:04:45.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and what happened\Nto that cool ship you had?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.45,0:04:49.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, now... We'll have\Nplenty of time for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.83,0:04:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll tell you all about it on the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.25,0:04:52.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.99,0:04:53.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.41,0:04:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Final draft! Project Robinson Ver 3.0
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.71,0:04:59.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Nagara, did you put all this\Ntogether? This is incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.12,0:05:02.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, if we take this... and do that...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.84,0:05:04.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,800)}There, it's perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.91,0:06:06.90,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.90,0:06:09.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Pretty handy, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.41,0:06:15.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, that is awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.91,0:06:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.87,0:06:20.92,Default,,0,0,0,,we're good here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.71,0:06:25.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Nagara!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.88,0:06:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you take it from here?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.05,0:06:30.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.23,0:06:39.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Mizuho.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.94,0:06:44.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not going to use that over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.98,0:06:48.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Nah, I can do what\NI need from here. Besides,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.25,0:06:52.99,Default,,0,0,0,,as long as I'm doing this,\NI want to watch it with my own eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.75,0:06:57.62,Default,,0,0,0,,So you really aren't going\Nto come home with us, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.08,0:07:00.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-mm. I'm staying here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.50,0:07:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Rajdhani, didn't you ever feel homesick?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.43,0:07:13.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You were all by yourself\Nfor 2,000 years, weren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.55,0:07:16.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Homesick... now there's\Na sensation that takes me back.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.40,0:07:19.35,Default,,0,0,0,,There was a world that I stopped by before
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.35,0:07:22.14,Default,,0,0,0,,that painted really close pictures\Nof scenes from my old home.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.65,0:07:27.90,Default,,0,0,0,,They were shockingly accurate and vivid,\Nbut most of all, mysterious.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.33,0:07:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,So much so that they made me feel uneasy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.99,0:07:35.65,Default,,0,0,0,,That was the first time since we went\Nadrift that I felt any sense of nostalgia.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.41,0:07:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I decided to call that\N{\i1}This {\i0}World "Homesick."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.79,0:07:43.29,Default,,0,0,0,,By "old home," do you mean\Nthe world we came from?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.29,0:07:46.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but also, kind of different.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.54,0:07:50.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The world was more "our-world-like"\Nthan it was "our world."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.79,0:07:55.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The master of that world was almost\Npathologically caught up in his memories,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.05,0:07:57.05,Default,,0,0,0,,and kept recreating his homeland.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.94,0:08:01.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The strange thing was,\Nno matter how far you went in this world,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.06,0:08:04.56,Default,,0,0,0,,there was never another soul\Nrepresented anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.03,0:08:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds like a lonely place.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.32,0:08:12.07,Default,,0,0,0,,But then, when a certain time approached,\Nthe style radically changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.07,0:08:14.74,Default,,0,0,0,,When I saw those images,\NI was taken aback.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.74,0:08:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,They were the likeness\Nof this one female student.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.78,0:08:21.12,Default,,0,0,0,,She was depicted as\Na real beauty, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.12,0:08:23.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Apparently, this girl\Nused to be his girlfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.09,0:08:26.37,Default,,0,0,0,,This is starting to get interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.50,0:08:29.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn't it? I gave in to my curiosity, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.84,0:08:32.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I took a look at her with my Scoop Scope,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.05,0:08:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,a power holdover that I developed myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.64,0:08:36.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and...?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.76,0:08:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The actual girl was not\Nnearly as pretty as her image.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.18,0:08:44.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Those love goggles come\Nwith a strong prescription.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.73,0:08:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,However, the girl really did love him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.73,0:08:52.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It got me curious,\Nso I peered into the other images.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.15,0:08:55.24,Default,,0,0,0,,His actual home was a town that I knew,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.24,0:08:59.90,Default,,0,0,0,,which wasn't as beautiful or nearly\Nas attractive as how he had depicted it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.33,0:09:04.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Put simply, he didn't accept reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.58,0:09:10.13,Default,,0,0,0,,His girlfriend wanted him to live\Nin the reality in front of his eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.13,0:09:14.38,Default,,0,0,0,,But he refused to change.\NSo eventually, she got fed up with him,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.38,0:09:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,and she left that world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.51,0:09:22.93,Default,,0,0,0,,So then he began painting pictures\Nof his girlfriend like a man possessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.93,0:09:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,That figure of her was\Nwhat was in the paintings.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.27,0:09:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,It felt as though I had been\Nunexpectedly confronted by reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.65,0:09:35.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought, can I say I'm actually\Nliving my own life in reality?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.15,0:09:41.24,Default,,0,0,0,,She didn't want to create\Nbeautiful memories with him;
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.24,0:09:45.45,Default,,0,0,0,,she wanted to create a future\Nwith him that was still unformed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.79,0:09:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,At some point, he became\Na captive to his memories of her,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.80,0:09:55.55,Default,,0,0,0,,and that became his entire world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.55,0:09:57.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Did he die?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.26,0:09:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, I'm not sure\Nexactly how to answer that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.05,0:10:03.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Death in {\i1}This {\i0}World is\Na little bit complicated.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.48,0:10:09.56,Default,,0,0,0,,When I think about dying,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.56,0:10:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,it's dark, and scary,\Nand makes my chest feel tight.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.03,0:10:16.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder if that's how\Nit was for Nozomi, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.04,0:10:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Did she feel afraid?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.50,0:10:32.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Nagara,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.79,0:10:35.17,Default,,0,0,0,,have you been to see\Nthe world where Nozomi died?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.63,0:10:37.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.01,0:10:40.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Then how were you able\Nto make certain that she died?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.18,0:10:45.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I see. Mizuho's cat, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.06,0:10:50.93,Default,,0,0,0,,She is able to tell...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.77,0:10:54.44,Default,,0,0,0,,...the status of {\i1}all {\i0}things.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.61,0:10:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,There was an inventor in one world.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.36,0:11:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The students who were in that world
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.28,0:11:04.49,Default,,0,0,0,,believed themselves to\Nbe the children of God,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.49,0:11:08.32,Default,,0,0,0,,and were convinced that they had\Nto keep their minds and bodies spotless.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.91,0:11:11.71,Default,,0,0,0,,They made up their minds\Nto live without killing,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.71,0:11:14.33,Default,,0,0,0,,without eating meat,\Nand to not even kill any plants.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.13,0:11:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,That was a world of fasting.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.67,0:11:20.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds like an awfully difficult world.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.59,0:11:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,No, actually, they seemed\Nsurprisingly happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.55,0:11:28.52,Default,,0,0,0,,That world flourished with a beautiful,\Nadvanced civilization,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.52,0:11:30.10,Default,,0,0,0,,and had a lot of\Nholdovers remaining in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.23,0:11:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, you don't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.36,0:11:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,For one thing,\Nhunger isn't that big a deal to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.20,0:11:42.20,Default,,0,0,0,,On the fringe of that world,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.20,0:11:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,there was a student who\Nwas obsessed with dying.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.95,0:11:50.16,Default,,0,0,0,,He was trying to produce\Ndeath here in this static world—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.16,0:11:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,an inventor of "death."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.13,0:11:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Invent "death"?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.08,0:11:59.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. He was trying to upset the stasis\Nof this world through people's deaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.05,0:12:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,To tell you the truth,\NI kind of admired him a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.39,0:12:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,His sense of morals aside, this was\Na challenge directed at {\i1}This {\i0}World.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.94,0:12:11.14,Default,,0,0,0,,But then...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.64,0:12:15.06,Default,,0,0,0,,...the actual guy was the devil himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.06,0:12:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,He reviled God, burned down the forests,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.90,0:12:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,wolfed down meat, and held\Nthose who fasted in contempt.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.90,0:12:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What's more, he took\Nadvantage of the stasis here
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.70,0:12:26.90,Default,,0,0,0,,to conduct experiments in suicide\Nand murder over and over.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.90,0:12:29.91,Default,,0,0,0,,This guy sounds like\Nnothing more than a serial killer.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.87,0:12:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. He was so utterly atrocious,\NI honestly felt like killing him myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.59,0:12:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,So then, finally, he invented "death."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.80,0:12:46.01,Default,,0,0,0,,He... apparently wanted to die so badly,\Nhe couldn't help himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.01,0:12:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,So he was the very first person\Nhe used his invention on.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.55,0:12:51.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And he died with flying colors.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.14,0:12:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.23,0:12:57.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm. I actually found his invention.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.11,0:13:01.19,Default,,0,0,0,,It was like...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.32,0:13:04.24,Default,,0,0,0,,...he was telling me to have a seat, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.82,0:13:07.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? Did you sit down?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.87,0:13:15.66,Default,,0,0,0,,He didn't look at all different\Nfrom who he was before he died.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.26,0:13:19.16,Default,,0,0,0,,But with each passing day,\Nthe changes began appearing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.29,0:13:23.17,Default,,0,0,0,,The inventor no longer had any desires.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.01,0:13:27.18,Default,,0,0,0,,He accepted what he saw in\Nfront of him, was content with it,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.18,0:13:30.72,Default,,0,0,0,,and no longer offered any\Ncriticism or hatred of anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.72,0:13:33.93,Default,,0,0,0,,He became a well-adjusted person,\Nnot unlike a Buddha.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.93,0:13:38.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The inventor had left {\i1}This {\i0}World.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.69,0:13:41.90,Default,,0,0,0,,He knew that when\Nhis drive came to an end,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.90,0:13:44.56,Default,,0,0,0,,it marked the end of his life as he was.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.56,0:13:48.57,Default,,0,0,0,,This is one form of "death" in {\i1}This {\i0}World.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.62,0:13:52.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I ended up not sitting down.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.07,0:13:55.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you suppose he hated himself?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.70,0:13:58.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Who knows? After all this time,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.62,0:14:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know why he was\Nso obsessed with dying.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.63,0:14:05.76,Default,,0,0,0,,But after living for so long,\NI understand something—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.76,0:14:08.84,Default,,0,0,0,,as you keep building up all sorts of\Nexperiences and what have you,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.84,0:14:11.55,Default,,0,0,0,,there's something about you\Nthat grows more and more irregular.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.93,0:14:16.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The larger it gets, the more\Nindividual meanings become diluted,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.23,0:14:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,and the more homogenized\Nthings become, I'd say.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.10,0:14:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I can tell that I'm steadily growing more\Napathetic the more unbalanced I get.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.57,0:14:26.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Ultimately, I'll end up as\Na gaping, lopsided hole.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.54,0:14:31.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm being drained away by time,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.82,0:14:34.99,Default,,0,0,0,,until someday, I'll become\Na mere shape, much like Nozomi has.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.99,0:14:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's nothing more than another\Nstate incorporated into this stasis.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.83,0:14:40.83,Default,,0,0,0,,If that can be called "death," then...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.83,0:14:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,...it's no different than\Nthe "death" in our own world.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.17,0:14:48.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. There's no such thing as a soul,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.47,0:14:51.84,Default,,0,0,0,,and our consciousness is born\Nfor no reason, then it just fades away.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.60,0:14:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Life is an endless\Nexercise in vain effort.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.14,0:15:00.44,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's precisely\Nbecause it's meaningless
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.44,0:15:04.35,Default,,0,0,0,,that I think the brilliance of\Nthis moment in life is so precious.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.24,0:15:09.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Because that one moment\Nbelongs to that person alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.87,0:15:11.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Nozomi isn't ever coming back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.46,0:15:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,But even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.09,0:15:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,...her will still lives on.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.88,0:15:33.67,Default,,0,0,0,,How much of it is finished?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.67,0:15:39.68,Default,,0,0,0,,The cats are doing their best,\Nbut I'd have to say about 20%.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.68,0:15:41.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I did try reaching out to the others...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.93,0:15:45.06,Default,,0,0,0,,...but they all said\Nthey weren't going back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.52,0:15:48.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It ended up being just\NMizuho and me... and...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.54,0:15:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,...Nozomi who were going.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.99,0:15:55.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Doing it like this means that\Nin going back to our own world,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.70,0:15:58.07,Default,,0,0,0,,we might end up not\Nbeing who we are anymore,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.07,0:15:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.45,0:16:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm. Plus the time it will take.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.21,0:16:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if we do make it back, two years\Nwill have passed since we went adrift.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.17,0:16:09.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And there's a chance\Nthat I'll be dead there.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.96,0:16:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.09,0:16:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, there's no use in thinking\Nabout what might happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.22,0:16:18.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I could just as well be alive, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.68,0:16:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything that took place here\Ncould end up as though it never happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.69,0:16:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,And if it does...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.15,0:16:25.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.10,0:16:26.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.82,0:16:29.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me, if we do get back...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.42,0:16:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,...what's the first thing you want to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.75,0:16:35.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't given that any thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.61,0:16:37.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not? It's fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.17,0:16:41.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I mean, we might not\Neven remember any of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.70,0:16:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And there's no use in thinking\Nabout what might happen, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.25,0:16:48.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? Then, are you calling me\Na fool for thinking so much about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.09,0:16:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just saying, it's not a big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.76,0:16:55.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Hm-hmm, you know what?\NI'm going to have a Soleil omu-rice,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.84,0:16:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,something with a ton\Nof grace strawberries on it,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.43,0:17:01.01,Default,,0,0,0,,then eat my fill of\NChinese noodles from Hatsune...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.01,0:17:05.39,Default,,0,0,0,,There, you see? I knew it.\NWhat a bunch of nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.40,0:17:08.77,Default,,0,0,0,,After that,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.77,0:17:11.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to find the\Ncurmudgeonly-looking boy
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.03,0:17:12.86,Default,,0,0,0,,from the corner of the staff room,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.86,0:17:15.40,Default,,0,0,0,,grab him by the scruff of the neck,\Nand ask him a question.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.62,0:17:19.07,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.74,0:17:24.32,Default,,0,0,0,,"Will you be my friend once again?"
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.12,0:17:29.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Once I do, what do you\Nsuppose he will answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.59,0:17:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We're already high-schoolers.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.80,0:17:35.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.84,0:17:37.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I just don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.51,0:17:39.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.01,0:17:41.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.64,0:17:44.80,Default,,0,0,0,,...you and me being friends\Nwill have never happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.60,0:17:48.44,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll have torn up your textbook again,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.44,0:17:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'll have abandoned that bird.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.02,0:17:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not true. We've made\Na lot of progress since then.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.49,0:17:59.32,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no telling\Nif what happened here...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.32,0:18:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,...will still have\Nhappened over there, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.92,0:18:04.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Still,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.82,0:18:08.04,Default,,0,0,0,,they {\i1}did {\i0}for sure happen here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.88,0:18:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, how about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.08,0:18:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Whichever one of us\Nremembers has to do as I say.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.38,0:18:19.96,Default,,0,0,0,,We have to become friends again.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.30,0:18:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay? Promise me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.39,0:18:25.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Promise me you won't refuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.31,0:18:29.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.19,0:18:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter how well I've come to understand
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.86,0:18:41.53,Default,,0,0,0,,the psychology of this universe, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.53,0:18:47.54,Default,,0,0,0,,...can't do anything more for a friend\Nwho's crying but sit next to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.42,0:18:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you...!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.18,0:19:04.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Rajdhani...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.06,0:19:06.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to ask you about something.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.97,0:19:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.94,0:19:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,There's one item I want\Nto add to Project Robinson.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.36,0:19:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, now we're talking.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.03,0:19:21.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I know we can't change the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.53,0:19:24.41,Default,,0,0,0,,In which case...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.54,0:19:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, analog-style.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.00,0:19:36.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Heh-heh, that's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.84,0:19:40.76,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the very same rocket that\Nfirst took mankind to the moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.76,0:19:41.96,Default,,0,0,0,,That's good luck, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.55,0:19:45.51,Default,,0,0,0,,The cat's copies are\Naccurately reproduced.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.51,0:19:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,And what's up top is even more primitive.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.39,0:19:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Mizuho,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.06,0:19:52.85,Default,,0,0,0,,why did you want to go home?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.44,0:19:56.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I... have things I want to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.94,0:19:59.86,Default,,0,0,0,,The cats can't live over there anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.65,0:20:03.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm. I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.49,0:20:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, it's pretty easy to\Nget back to our own world.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.33,0:20:13.74,Default,,0,0,0,,But to do so requires\Nresolve and sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.46,0:20:16.54,Default,,0,0,0,,We can't get back\Nthe time that has passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.54,0:20:19.67,Default,,0,0,0,,But you two can still make it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.30,0:20:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Still, we're not simply\Ngoing back, are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.88,0:20:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Right. Nagara is...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.76,0:20:28.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry I'm late.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.22,0:20:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Now everything is ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.06,0:20:34.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow is the big day.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.66,0:20:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I've had enough already.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.36,0:20:43.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm staying here with the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.99,0:20:48.53,Default,,0,0,0,,If you ever happen to run into me,\Nit would be my pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.53,0:20:50.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.37,0:20:53.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.37,0:20:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I'll take care of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.88,0:20:59.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks for everything you've done.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.42,0:21:03.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Yamabiko, you take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.64,0:21:09.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Sakura! See you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.39,0:21:13.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to go now!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.40,0:21:17.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.36,0:21:19.89,Default,,0,0,0,,...left my cats behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.15,0:21:25.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure the cats feel the same as we do.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.95,0:21:32.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder if Sakura will\Nwatch over them, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.12,0:21:34.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.25,0:21:38.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Fifteen seconds to launch.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.16,0:21:39.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Switching to internal power.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.43,0:21:41.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Twelve...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.43,0:21:43.88,Default,,0,0,0,,...eleven... ten...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.88,0:21:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,,...nine...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.93,0:21:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Ignition start.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.20,0:22:15.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Launch pad safely cleared\Nand you are on course.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.17,0:22:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That's all the support I can give you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.96,0:22:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.17,0:22:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Copy. Farewell, Rajdhani.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.30,0:22:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, now then...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.18,0:22:37.22,Default,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.53,0:22:40.56,Default,,0,0,0,,...must be from Mizuho. Then, this...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.40,0:22:48.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing matters in {\i1}This {\i0}World...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.70,0:22:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,...but once in a while,\Ncool things do happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.41,0:22:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,That is why I can get by.
